--- body ---
## Context

Every paid call of the Observer runs under a declared budget, reads its key
at use only, and reaches a hosted model only for a document that allows it,
with retention off. No ticket carried this. Normative text, accepted
specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):

- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 7 (budgets declared in the run report header,
  enforced by the run; proposed defaults in § 7.2: USD 3 per document,
  USD 20 per ordinary batch, USD 60 for the full M2 pass, monthly and
  per-vendor caps, GPU time; "Reaching a budget"); the amounts are the
  author's to set (§ 13, default: the table as proposed).
- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 6 (secrets: provider key files, the reading
  rule through `scripts/pipeline_keystore.py`, missing key, leak); § 5
  "What reaches a hosted model" and "Every call is recorded"; § 8 (spend and
  compute time in the run report, monthly tally).
- `docs/jetp-requirements.md` C4 (budgets), C9 (secrets), Q15 (cost and
  effort measured).

Blocked by [[1875]], which writes the run report whose header declares the
budgets and whose body records the spend.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A run declares its budgets in its report header; a paid call that would pass the per-document, per-run, monthly or per-vendor budget is not made, and the run stops or leaves the document pending as operation § 7.2 "Reaching a budget" says (red tests replaying the USD 20 and the per-vendor checks of operation § 14)
- [ ] A run never switches vendor to stay under a budget (red test)
- [ ] Every LLM call records run, LLM identifier, prompt version, sampling settings where exposed, tokens in and out, and cost in USD; a local call records wall time and GPU time at zero cost
- [ ] A monthly tally of spend per vendor and GPU time is computed from the run reports
- [ ] Every credential is read at use through `scripts/pipeline_keystore.py` or a process-scoped substitution; a run whose key is missing stops before its first paid call and names the provider; a test shows no run report contains a credential (C9)
- [ ] No hosted call is made for a `local_only` document; every hosted call requests no data collection and zero retention, goes only to an endpoint that honours them and fails closed otherwise; the run records the settings and the endpoint (red test)
- [ ] The author sets the budget amounts, or the defaults of operation § 7.2 stand, recorded here
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
